<div class="flex_column av-74ej-6cf5339ddc04e86d9cee708b796d5524 av_one_full avia-builder-el-50 el_after_av_section el_before_av_section avia-builder-el-no-sibling first flex_column_div"><div class="av-special-heading av-m4eco7jk-9e4daa735c73ee441fdb8a8a26afcc7f av-special-heading-h3 custom-color-heading blockquote modern-quote modern-centered avia-builder-el-51 el_before_av_toggle_container avia-builder-el-first av-inherit-size"><h3 class="av-special-heading-tag" itemprop="headline">Frequently Asked Questions</h3><div class="special-heading-border"><div class="special-heading-inner-border"></div></div></div>
<div class="togglecontainer av-m4ecs2t0-75d86485974b4316a3dcd52820fe8607 av-elegant-toggle avia-builder-el-52 el_after_av_heading avia-builder-el-last toggle_close_all enable_toggles" itemscope="itemscope" itemtype="https://schema.org/FAQPage">
<section class="av_toggle_section av-m4ecpiju-7086f60bb440afa6b79e7c4daa059ee5" itemprop="mainEntity" itemscope="itemscope" itemtype="https://schema.org/Question"><div class="single_toggle" data-tags="{All} " role="tablist"><p aria-controls="toggle-id-1" aria-expanded="false" aria-label="Click to expand: What is Transcranial Magnetic Stimulation?" class="toggler av-title-above" data-aria_collapsed="Click to expand: What is Transcranial Magnetic Stimulation?" data-aria_expanded="Click to collapse: What is Transcranial Magnetic Stimulation?" data-fake-id="#toggle-id-1" data-slide-speed="200" data-title="What is Transcranial Magnetic Stimulation?" data-title-open="" id="toggle-toggle-id-1" itemprop="name" role="tab" tabindex="0">What is Transcranial Magnetic Stimulation?<span class="toggle_icon"><span class="vert_icon"></span><span class="hor_icon"></span></span></p><div aria-hidden="true" aria-labelledby="toggle-toggle-id-1" class="toggle_wrap av-title-above" id="toggle-id-1" itemprop="acceptedAnswer" itemscope="itemscope" itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer" role="region" tabindex="-1"><div class="toggle_content invers-color" itemprop="text"><p>TMS is a non-invasive procedure that uses magnetic fields to stimulate nerve cells in the brain to improve symptoms of depression, typically used when antidepressant medications haven’t been effective.</p>
</div></div></div></section>
<section class="av_toggle_section av-m4ecptnh-5e88473d48b484ce5c1326110beeb8aa" itemprop="mainEntity" itemscope="itemscope" itemtype="https://schema.org/Question"><div class="single_toggle" data-tags="{All} " role="tablist"><p aria-controls="toggle-id-2" aria-expanded="false" aria-label="Click to expand: How does TMS work?" class="toggler av-title-above" data-aria_collapsed="Click to expand: How does TMS work?" data-aria_expanded="Click to collapse: How does TMS work?" data-fake-id="#toggle-id-2" data-slide-speed="200" data-title="How does TMS work?" data-title-open="" id="toggle-toggle-id-2" itemprop="name" role="tab" tabindex="0">How does TMS work?<span class="toggle_icon"><span class="vert_icon"></span><span class="hor_icon"></span></span></p><div aria-hidden="true" aria-labelledby="toggle-toggle-id-2" class="toggle_wrap av-title-above" id="toggle-id-2" itemprop="acceptedAnswer" itemscope="itemscope" itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer" role="region" tabindex="-1"><div class="toggle_content invers-color" itemprop="text"><p>TMS involves delivering magnetic pulses to specific parts of the brain.</p>
</div></div></div></section>
<section class="av_toggle_section av-m4ecq5kb-473f9d7a96c4077c2a01bf4e6773bbec" itemprop="mainEntity" itemscope="itemscope" itemtype="https://schema.org/Question"><div class="single_toggle" data-tags="{All} " role="tablist"><p aria-controls="toggle-id-3" aria-expanded="false" aria-label="Click to expand: How long is NeuroStar TMS Treatment?" class="toggler av-title-above" data-aria_collapsed="Click to expand: How long is NeuroStar TMS Treatment?" data-aria_expanded="Click to collapse: How long is NeuroStar TMS Treatment?" data-fake-id="#toggle-id-3" data-slide-speed="200" data-title="How long is NeuroStar TMS Treatment?" data-title-open="" id="toggle-toggle-id-3" itemprop="name" role="tab" tabindex="0">How long is NeuroStar TMS Treatment?<span class="toggle_icon"><span class="vert_icon"></span><span class="hor_icon"></span></span></p><div aria-hidden="true" aria-labelledby="toggle-toggle-id-3" class="toggle_wrap av-title-above" id="toggle-id-3" itemprop="acceptedAnswer" itemscope="itemscope" itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer" role="region" tabindex="-1"><div class="toggle_content invers-color" itemprop="text"><p>A typical initial course of treatment is about 19-37 minutes daily over 4-6 weeks.</p>
</div></div></div></section>
<section class="av_toggle_section av-m4ecqv7c-4bec190223e4fdb20aafd962ca2c530d" itemprop="mainEntity" itemscope="itemscope" itemtype="https://schema.org/Question"><div class="single_toggle" data-tags="{All} " role="tablist"><p aria-controls="toggle-id-4" aria-expanded="false" aria-label="Click to expand: Is TMS Therapy a good alternative for patients who cannot tolerate the side effects of antidepressant medications?" class="toggler av-title-above" data-aria_collapsed="Click to expand: Is TMS Therapy a good alternative for patients who cannot tolerate the side effects of antidepressant medications?" data-aria_expanded="Click to collapse: Is TMS Therapy a good alternative for patients who cannot tolerate the side effects of antidepressant medications?" data-fake-id="#toggle-id-4" data-slide-speed="200" data-title="Is TMS Therapy a good alternative for patients who cannot tolerate the side effects of antidepressant medications?" data-title-open="" id="toggle-toggle-id-4" itemprop="name" role="tab" tabindex="0">Is TMS Therapy a good alternative for patients who cannot tolerate the side effects of antidepressant medications?<span class="toggle_icon"><span class="vert_icon"></span><span class="hor_icon"></span></span></p><div aria-hidden="true" aria-labelledby="toggle-toggle-id-4" class="toggle_wrap av-title-above" id="toggle-id-4" itemprop="acceptedAnswer" itemscope="itemscope" itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer" role="region" tabindex="-1"><div class="toggle_content invers-color" itemprop="text"><p>Yes, a TMS depression treatment session does not circulate in the blood throughout the body, avoiding systemic side effects like weight gain, sexual dysfunction, and nausea.</p>
</div></div></div></section>
<section class="av_toggle_section av-m4ecr6xu-bfbe3f2504bda8ccc1c830295f75795d" itemprop="mainEntity" itemscope="itemscope" itemtype="https://schema.org/Question"><div class="single_toggle" data-tags="{All} " role="tablist"><p aria-controls="toggle-id-5" aria-expanded="false" aria-label="Click to expand: Is TMS Therapy like other alternative therapies that use magnets?" class="toggler av-title-above" data-aria_collapsed="Click to expand: Is TMS Therapy like other alternative therapies that use magnets?" data-aria_expanded="Click to collapse: Is TMS Therapy like other alternative therapies that use magnets?" data-fake-id="#toggle-id-5" data-slide-speed="200" data-title="Is TMS Therapy like other alternative therapies that use magnets?" data-title-open="" id="toggle-toggle-id-5" itemprop="name" role="tab" tabindex="0">Is TMS Therapy like other alternative therapies that use magnets?<span class="toggle_icon"><span class="vert_icon"></span><span class="hor_icon"></span></span></p><div aria-hidden="true" aria-labelledby="toggle-toggle-id-5" class="toggle_wrap av-title-above" id="toggle-id-5" itemprop="acceptedAnswer" itemscope="itemscope" itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer" role="region" tabindex="-1"><div class="toggle_content invers-color" itemprop="text"><p>No, TMS Therapy for anxiety, depression, and other mental health disorders uses pulsed magnetic fields that are much stronger and directed compared to the static magnetic fields used in other products.</p>
</div></div></div></section>
<section class="av_toggle_section av-m4ecrgo7-969d4db6ca55b068d2ad845722121613" itemprop="mainEntity" itemscope="itemscope" itemtype="https://schema.org/Question"><div class="single_toggle" data-tags="{All} " role="tablist"><p aria-controls="toggle-id-6" aria-expanded="false" aria-label="Click to expand: Does it work?" class="toggler av-title-above" data-aria_collapsed="Click to expand: Does it work?" data-aria_expanded="Click to collapse: Does it work?" data-fake-id="#toggle-id-6" data-slide-speed="200" data-title="Does it work?" data-title-open="" id="toggle-toggle-id-6" itemprop="name" role="tab" tabindex="0">Does it work?<span class="toggle_icon"><span class="vert_icon"></span><span class="hor_icon"></span></span></p><div aria-hidden="true" aria-labelledby="toggle-toggle-id-6" class="toggle_wrap av-title-above" id="toggle-id-6" itemprop="acceptedAnswer" itemscope="itemscope" itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer" role="region" tabindex="-1"><div class="toggle_content invers-color" itemprop="text"><p>In a study of “real-world” outcomes (meaning actual NeuroStar patients), 83% of people who completed the full NeuroStar treatment cycle experienced a measurable decrease in the severity of their depression, and 62% of those completing treatment saw full remission – meaning their depression effectively “went away.”</p>
</div></div></div></section>
<section class="av_toggle_section av-m4ecrq6s-d80e14c98f337be80172a47c76e40d49" itemprop="mainEntity" itemscope="itemscope" itemtype="https://schema.org/Question"><div class="single_toggle" data-tags="{All} " role="tablist"><p aria-controls="toggle-id-7" aria-expanded="false" aria-label="Click to expand: Does it hurt?" class="toggler av-title-above" data-aria_collapsed="Click to expand: Does it hurt?" data-aria_expanded="Click to collapse: Does it hurt?" data-fake-id="#toggle-id-7" data-slide-speed="200" data-title="Does it hurt?" data-title-open="" id="toggle-toggle-id-7" itemprop="name" role="tab" tabindex="0">Does it hurt?<span class="toggle_icon"><span class="vert_icon"></span><span class="hor_icon"></span></span></p><div aria-hidden="true" aria-labelledby="toggle-toggle-id-7" class="toggle_wrap av-title-above" id="toggle-id-7" itemprop="acceptedAnswer" itemscope="itemscope" itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer" role="region" tabindex="-1"><div class="toggle_content invers-color" itemprop="text"><p>While there may be some minor discomfort at the treatment site (where the device touches your head), it generally subsides within the first week of treatment. There is no sedation or impact on your alertness. You can read, watch TV, or talk with your treatment coordinator during your session, and you can drive home immediately after treatment.</p>
</div></div></div></section>
<section class="av_toggle_section av-m4ecs14j-072a65005e3bf629f059c7049a3f9f54" itemprop="mainEntity" itemscope="itemscope" itemtype="https://schema.org/Question"><div class="single_toggle" data-tags="{All} " role="tablist"><p aria-controls="toggle-id-8" aria-expanded="false" aria-label="Click to expand: Does insurance cover it?" class="toggler av-title-above" data-aria_collapsed="Click to expand: Does insurance cover it?" data-aria_expanded="Click to collapse: Does insurance cover it?" data-fake-id="#toggle-id-8" data-slide-speed="200" data-title="Does insurance cover it?" data-title-open="" id="toggle-toggle-id-8" itemprop="name" role="tab" tabindex="0">Does insurance cover it?<span class="toggle_icon"><span class="vert_icon"></span><span class="hor_icon"></span></span></p><div aria-hidden="true" aria-labelledby="toggle-toggle-id-8" class="toggle_wrap av-title-above" id="toggle-id-8" itemprop="acceptedAnswer" itemscope="itemscope" itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer" role="region" tabindex="-1"><div class="toggle_content invers-color" itemprop="text"><p>Over 300 million people have insurance plans that cover NeuroStar, including Medicare and Tricare. Conditions and coverage can vary by insurance company, and your NeuroStar Team Lead will help you determine your benefits and coverage. We also offer cash-pay and patient financing options if desired. Talk with your NeuroStar representative for more details.</p>
</div></div></div></section>
